Description: qt: a 3D still is read as its pair, through the stereo layer
 The image producer asks Sparky Stereo OS's stereo layer (1.23) for a still:
 JPS, MPO, PNG with sTER, or a pair by the layer's photo policy. A 3D still is
 given as its two views side by side, the left eye first, and the producer says
 so (meta.media.stereo3d.type side_by_side, views full), so an editor takes it
 as any full side-by-side clip. An MPO, two pictures in one file, is no longer
 refused as an animation. A 2D picture is read as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
